module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_moved_or_copied_block_uses_a_name_the_mover_never_imported

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungRead, FoundBelowTheLadder, FoundOnRung, BelowCeiling }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable, Mitigatable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_moved_or_copied_block_uses_a_name_the_mover_never_imported: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_moved_or_copied_block_uses_a_name_the_mover_never_imported" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder,
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "a resolve-time refusal that names, per block, every declaration the body uses that its import list does not carry -- the refusal the call-site position already produces (a call whose callee identity cannot be established) applied to annotation and constructor positions too -- with discriminating REDs enrolled (a body using an unimported type name; a body whose import list repeats a name) and a positive control (a block whose imports are exactly its body's needs), on the required path; plus, on the mover side, the capability for a mechanical split to derive a moved block's import list from the identifiers in that block rather than from a list the mover maintains by hand.",
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "**a data block that was moved or copied out of its module keeps a name it never imported, and the compiler refuses it in one position and tolerates it in another**. INVALID STATE: a block whose body names a declaration its import list does not carry. HARM: the silent half. Where the body CALLS the name, resolve stops the build (`call to '<name>' has no established callee identity`, so its effects cannot be joined -- a loud, correct refusal). Where the body only USES the name as a type annotation or a constructor in a literal, nothing refuses, and the block is mergeable, testable and wrong: the name it needs is not there, and the next reader pays for it in the first fold that needs the callee. The import list is unchecked in both directions, so a name can also be listed twice inside one list and parse clean (measured).",

    "SIGHTING ONE, on main: `test.claim.long.decl_ref_resolution_witness` imported `std.decl_ref`'s three types (`DeclarationRef`, `WholeDeclaration`, `NamedField`) and never the function `decl_ref`, while its body called `decl_ref(module_path:, decl_name:)`. Six claims in that file failed at resolve with `call to 'decl_ref' has no established callee identity`, and the file was carried as a frozen-path deferral in `gunbc.witness.witness_deferral_freeze` `frozen_path_deferrals` rather than fixed. The instrument for finding citations that resolve to nothing was itself written with a reference nothing resolved. Fixed on main by `e517c969b4d` (#16641) -- one line, the missing import.",

    "SIGHTING TWO, this lane, on mechanically split rows: splitting the integration-concern register into one file per concern (`gunbc.integration_concern`, gunb-ai/gunbc#16338) generated row files with an import list seeded from a list of known union variants rather than from the block being moved. A concern whose body calls `std.decl_ref`'s `decl_field_ref` therefore arrived without that import, and the reading fold refused it exactly as main's witness was refused. The same sweep found five more rows ported at earlier merges carrying used-but-unimported names -- `CommitSha`, `HistoricalDeclaration`, `IntegrationEvidence`, `RetainedExecutionResult`, and `IntegrationConcern` on the block's own type annotation -- all of them in the SILENT position, all of them merged, tested and shipped, plus one name listed twice in a single import list. Repaired in `1b9b7d3400e`; no field text moved.",

    "WHAT MAKES THIS A CLASS AND NOT TWO COINCIDENCES: both instances were GENERATED BY A MOVE, not written next to their use, and in both the mover's notion of what to carry was a maintained list rather than a read of the block. A hand-written file gets its imports beside the code that needs them and the omission shows up as the loud refusal at first write; a moved or copied block arrives with whatever the mover thought of, and lands in the tolerated position where no check looks. Second: neither instance was caught by a typecheck or a field comparison -- the field-by-field audit over 78 rows passed the whole time, because the fields were always right -- and both were caught only by RUNNING a fold over the directory. Any lane that ports rows, splits a module, or copies a block between modules is the next instance.",

    "RUNG NOW: found below the ladder; currently mitigatable, and mitigated per instance by hand (one import line each, `e517c969b4d` upstream and `1b9b7d3400e` here). Not mechanically preventable, because the only refusal the compiler offers is the callee-identity one, and it fires on call sites alone: the annotation and constructor positions carry the same defect invisibly, so nothing stops the next moved block from merging broken. No required-path step runs a check that a block's imports cover its body, and no workflow reference exists for one.",

    "CEILING: mechanically preventable, not structurally guaranteed. The refusal already exists and is exact -- resolve can say which name has no established callee identity -- so extending it to every position where a body names a declaration outside its import list is a mechanical act inside the phase that already resolves these names; a block literal remains constructible, which is what keeps this below structurally guaranteed. BLOCKER: climbable but unbuilt -- nothing is awaited from another authority, the check has simply not been written. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER (a capability, per gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder ob.3): the refusal above with its discriminating REDs and a positive control enrolled on the required path, and a mover-side capability for a split to derive a block's imports from the block itself. Until then every split re-donates this class, and the discovery mechanism remains 'someone runs a fold and reads the error'.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
